ZTEXT0010000210bcac7fef00000000
Zero Inspect - original header cards, idea723

Usage
  zero-inspect FILE
  zero-inspect.exe FILE

Native Linux x86-64 and Windows x86-64 command. The command accepts exactly
one path; extension and filename do not select the format. It opens an existing
regular file read-only, obtains its size, reads its signature and only the
required header, checks the size again, and closes it before printing a card.
Nothing is written to the input and no executable payload is run. A path can
contain spaces or UTF-8 characters when passed as one command-line argument.
The software's messages and card labels are English; row numbers start at1.

The program reads at most4096 bytes: 32 for Ztext,64 for Zpix/Zpack/Zapp,
4096 for Zmedia. Unknown signatures need only8 bytes. Workspace is110000
bytes, including the shared validator's continuation stack. File size does
not affect workspace size. No whole-file allocation, decoding, extraction,
process launcher, external runtime or payload scan is used.

Successful output ends with Header checked and Content checksum not checked.
For Zapp the more precise message is Content checksum: not present in this
format, followed by Executable content not checked; application was not run.
For Zpack the additional message is Index checksum, paths and entries not
checked. A successful card is NOT an integrity certificate, a trust decision,
or a promise that the file can be opened, rendered, extracted or executed.
Concurrent same-size content changes cannot be detected by this header-only
reader. The file should remain unchanged while it is inspected.

Header contracts
All binary integers below are unsigned little-endian. Offsets are technical
byte offsets from the file start; they are not visible list numbering.

ZTEXT001,32-byte header, format version1 encoded in the signature:
  8..15 payload byte count as8 lowercase hexadecimal ASCII digits.
  16..23 declared FNV1a32 as8 lowercase hexadecimal ASCII digits.
  24..30 seven ASCII zeroes,31 LF. Payload0..1048576 bytes.
  Actual file bytes must equal32+payload. UTF-8, forbidden NUL and FNV are
  not checked. Card reports declared payload and derived expected total.

ZPIX0001,64-byte header, format version1 encoded in the signature:
  u32 width8:1..3840; height12:1..2160; channels16=3; encoding20=1.
  u64 pixels24=width*height; encoded payload32; full length48.
  u32 checksum40, reserved44=0; u64 reserved56=0.
  Actual bytes68..33554432; payload=actual-64 and divisible by4.
  The number of4-byte run records cannot exceed pixels, and255 times that
  number cannot be smaller than pixels. This rejects impossible lengths.
  RGB run contents and decoded-RGB checksum are not checked. Card includes
  dimensions, channel count and encoding; encoding is not mislabeled version.

ZPACK001,64-byte header:
  u64 version8=1; files16:0..4096; index bytes24=files*288;
  complete archive bytes32; index FNV1a32 stored in u64 at40;
  u64 reserved48=0,56=0. FNV upper32 bits must be zero.
  Actual bytes64..67108864 and equal declared complete length. Index must
  fit after the header. With zero files, actual length must be exactly64.
  Index checksum, entry paths, offsets, flags and file checksums are not
  checked. Card distinguishes complete archive size and derived payload.

ZMEDIA01,4096-byte header:
  u64 version8=1; header bytes16=4096; sector bytes24=512;
  payload bytes32:512..268435456, divisible by512; flags40=0.
  Bytes48..79 hold declared SHA256; bytes80..4095 must all be zero.
  Actual file bytes must equal4096+payload. SHA256 and bootability are not
  checked. The maximum image is inspected with the same bounded workspace.

ZEROAPP1,64-byte header, format version1 encoded in the signature:
  u64 architecture8=32 or64; complete image bytes16; entry offset24=64;
  minimum stack bytes32=4198400; ABI version40=1; reserved48=0,56=0.
  Complete length must equal actual length and exceed64. No universal size
  ceiling is invented: individual loaders impose their own buffer limits.
  There is no checksum field. The minimum stack field is not a load address.
  Card reports architecture, ABI, entry offset and required stack bytes.

Exit contract
  0  Supported signature and consistent header/length; payload unchecked.
  64 Wrong argument count or unavailable host platform.
  65 Unknown signature, truncated header, unsupported format version or
     architecture, malformed field/reserved bytes or inconsistent length.
  66 Input cannot be opened as an accessible regular file.
  74 Size/read/close/stdout failure, early EOF or detected file-size change.
Malformed input never prints Header checked or partially trusted metadata.
Errors are English text on stdout; callers should also inspect the exit code.
The underlying own file API rejects final links/reparse points recognized by
the host; ancestor directory links are outside that API's guarantee. Wine's
Z: mapping can expose a Unix symlink as an ordinary Windows file. This is not
a path-confinement tool and does not claim to detect that emulation behavior.

Original source and shared regression tests
  tools/inspect-head.zero.part   descriptor, bounded workspace and locals
  tools/inspect-worker.zero.part same memory-only validator in both programs
  tools/inspect-cli.zero.part    file reading and card output
  tools/inspect-check-main.zero.part test cases and fixture creation
  tools/inspect-compose.zero    original source composer, stdout only
  tools/inspect.zero            composed CLI source
  tools/inspect-check.zero      composed test source

Compile the composer with the existing own Zero compiler. From project root:
  inspect-compose tools/inspect-head.zero.part tools/inspect-worker.zero.part
    tools/inspect-cli.zero.part > tools/inspect.zero
  inspect-compose tools/inspect-head.zero.part tools/inspect-worker.zero.part
    tools/inspect-check-main.zero.part > tools/inspect-check.zero
Each displayed composer invocation is one command, wrapped here for reading.
Use zero --host or zero --windows with the composed source on stdin.
The composer does not invoke a compiler or any other program itself.

Run zero-inspect-check with no arguments for13757 shared-parser checks.
An optional NEW_DIRECTORY runs the same checks and writes36 fixtures there,
using exclusive creation and preserving existing directories/files. Six base
fixtures use extension .renamed: text, picture, archive, media, app64, app32.
Each has .bad-header, .bad-length, .bad-magic and .truncated variants, plus
.unchecked-content. The last intentionally corrupts an unchecked checksum
or application byte and MUST still receive a header-only card. Fixtures are
generated by Zero, not copied from a third-party codec or runtime.

The suite checks every header-byte corruption, every available-header
truncation and every actual-file truncation of the canonical fixtures.
It covers empty text/archive, maximum text/image/archive/media bounds,
count4096/4097, overflow-sized count/index/payload, invalid hex, impossible
RLE record counts, both app architectures and u64-limit app sizes without
large allocations. Repeated valid/invalid calls also check output resets.

