  Linux: missing/extra args, missing file, directory, final symlink and
  unreadable file returned64/66 as appropriate. Full stdout and injected
  read EIO, early EOF and close EIO returned74:10 CLI/I/O cases total.
  Wine: missing/extra args, missing file and directory returned64/66.
  Wine fixture creation and inspection succeeded in a path containing
  Cyrillic letters and spaces. Backslash Windows paths were also checked.
  Linux syscall trace of a real18878464-byte Zmedia showed only8+4088
  input bytes read. Existing text, picture, archive and both app headers
  were inspected without modification.
Windows evidence is Wine compatibility testing, not a native Windows
machine or hardware test. Unix symlink behavior through Wine is documented
above; no native Windows reparse-point test is claimed. Linux syscall fault
injection and Wine are external validation tools, not shipped dependencies.

